<Layout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	meta_title="Privacy Policy & Data Transparency | ErrorLedger"
	description="Data telemetry, cookie policies, AdSense disclosures, and user rights for ErrorLedger."
	pubDate={new Date('August 17, 2026')}
	tags={["legal", "privacy", "compliance"]}
>
	<p><em>Last Updated: August 17, 2026</em></p>

	<p>At ErrorLedger, we value transparency and privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how information is collected, used, and protected when you access the ErrorLedger platform.</p>

	<h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
	<p>When you visit ErrorLedger, we collect standard server telemetry to ensure uptime, security, and performance:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Log File Telemetry:</strong> Internet Protocol (IP) addresses, browser type, Internet Service Provider (ISP), date/time stamps, referring/exit pages, and click paths.</li>
		<li><strong>Local Browser Storage (localStorage):</strong> We use client-side storage solely to record your Reader Verdict poll votes, dark/light theme preference, and anonymous incident intake drafts on your own device.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>2. Advertising & Third-Party Cookies (Google AdSense)</h2>
	<p>ErrorLedger partners with third-party vendors, including Google, to serve advertisements when you visit our website:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Google uses cookies (such as the DoubleClick DART cookie) to serve ads to users based on their visits to this site and other sites on the internet.</li>
		<li>Users may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a> or through the <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Digital Advertising Alliance Consumer Choice page</a>.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>3. Anonymous Incident Submissions</h2>
	<p>
		When you submit an incident via our intake portal:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>We do not require you to provide your name, phone number, or employer identification.</li>
		<li>All submitted text is reviewed under our Whistleblower Protection standard to scrub sensitive identifiers prior to editorial publication.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>4. External Links</h2>
	<p>
		Our investigative case files contain links to public court records, news archives, and regulatory disclosures. ErrorLedger is not responsible for the privacy practices or content of these external domains.
	</p>

	<h2>5. Contact Information</h2>
	<p>
		For any questions, corrections, or privacy inquiries, contact us at <a href="mailto:contact@errorledger.com">contact@errorledger.com</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>